#Other Information
#Environmental Parameters (and sensors to which they are applied)
#Hole Size 		: 8.5" (all sensors)
#Tool Size 			: 6.75"
#Mud Type 		: WBM (Gamma Ray)
#Mud Weight 		: 1.25 - 1.30 SG (Gamma Ray)
#KCl Concentration by Weight 	: 4.21 - 5.05 pbw (Gamma Ray)
#Mud Resistivity at BHT 	: 0.07  ohmm @101.9 degC (Resistivity)
#Fluid Density 		: 1.00 g/cc (Density)
#Neutron Tool Lithology	: Limestone (Porosity)
#Whole Mud Chlorides 	: 28800 - 33426 ppm (Porosity)
#Formation Water Salinity 	: 20000 ppm Cl- (Porosity)
#Pressure and Temperature 	: from PWD and EWR (Density, Porosity)
#
#Comments:
#1) All depth are calibrated to the drillers pipe tally and are measured from drill floor.
#2) No depth correction have been made for pipe stretch or compression.
#3) LWD Resistivity Tool utilized in this run is EWRP4, with spacing configuration as below:
#    - Deep Resistivity = 39in Spacing / 1 Mhz Frequency
#    - Medium Resistivity = 27in Spacing / 2 MHz Frequency
#    - Shallow Resistivity = 15in Spacing / 2 MHz Frequency
#    - XShallow Resistivity = 9in Spacing /2 MHz Frequency
#4) CTN Alloy type used for CTN data processing is Mid Nickle.
#5) Density reading might be affected by detector standoff to borehole wall while sliding.
#6) All data presented is Memory data unless otherwise stated.
